### 4. Brick 8: Branch Extraction

#### [NEW] [branch_extraction.py](file:///c:/Users/geoal/Documents/SoftwareDev/PS_LiDAR/src/core/branch_extraction.py)

Extracción de ramas a partir de los troncos detectados:

```python
@dataclass
class BranchExtractionConfig:
    linearity_threshold: float = 0.5
    verticality_scale: float = 0.1       # m
    connectivity_radius: float = 0.15    # m
    max_branch_length: float = 5.0       # m - from field
    voxel_resolution: float = 0.05       # m
    min_branch_points: int = 50

@dataclass
class BranchExtractionResult:
    wood_mask: np.ndarray        # (N,) bool - trunk + branches
    branch_only_mask: np.ndarray # (N,) bool - only branches
    n_branch_clusters: int

def extract_branches(
    xyz: np.ndarray,
    trunk_result: TrunkExtractionResult,
    config: BranchExtractionConfig = None,
    verbose: bool = False,
) -> BranchExtractionResult:
    """
    Pipeline:
    1. Compute linearity (pgeof) on non-trunk points
    2. Filter by linearity threshold
    3. Voxelize candidates
    4. Build connectivity graph (26-neighbors)
    5. Connected components
    6. Keep only components connected to trunk
    7. Filter by max_branch_length from nearest trunk point
    """
```

